{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/60011-personal-projects","id":60011,"title":"Personal Projects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-28T11:57:28-08:00","id":60011,"title":"Personal Projects","content":"Anybody here doing personal projects that aren't fan material for WW/OPP games? I'm not asking people to go into details (unless they want to), I'm just curious to see what people might be working on. A couple of my projects are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1. The Daimyo Adventures: Based on a dream I had a while ago, it's basically a space fantasy game (still working on which system to do it for) that centers on players belonging to a large mobile space base that could basically operate it and a sizable fleet of spaceships. They are trying to stop a mummy sorceror who never quite gave up on the idea of slavery as a good thing (along with all of his cohorts and allies) from undoing the recent legislation that gave clones and cybernetic intelligences all the rights of people. Also, they have to contend with space kaiju.<br /> <br /> 2. A novel set in a world where every governement in the world collapsed in on themselves, and only corporations (some good, some bad) act as defacto governments. It's a bit of a war story between two major corporations, one with a libertarian sense of how things should go and one that took pages from the cyberpunk on how to be a megacorp.<br /> <br /> 3. Mecha Imperium (there is a reason I try to convince others for names on things): Another space fantasy where magic works best through giant robots. Basically me trying to create a table top version of Super Robot Wars as an RPG.<br /> <br /> 4. Another game featuring a &quot;modern&quot; war against mythological beings and humanity. Humanity is decidedly the bad guys and the players take on the role of mystical transhumans trying to see the world survives the mess.<br /> <br /> So, anyone have anything they are willing to share?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1575_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T16:20:21-08:00","id":67463,"title":"","content":"I got something on my own<br /> 1. The Fate: A complete world for a D&amp;D ambientation system, with history, complex political situations and lot of things. Actually, the main problem is that I don't know how contact the WotC in a decent way (as my english is rather poor).<br /> <br /> 2. A strategic-roleplay game with mecha, aircrafts, tank and so on. I already got the tabletop version, but it's so complex that it would be more feasible a computer version <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> 3. Another strategic game on the pattern of Space Empire IV (not V), but with some interesting changes. And more tacticism (ok, I need to become a god-like programmer, but I swear that, one day, I'll do it).<br /> <br /> 4. A zombie game, already half-done, I need to beta-test it, adjust it, and then try to produce it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the WW-things (yeah, I'm OT, but anyway...) <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElemen