:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T09:24:26-08:00","id":67938,"title":"","content":"I have the beginning of a novel which I think could be quite a good read, but after doing a bit of research on the market today it doesn't sound like I could live off writing alone and still be happy. Maybe I'll do e-books instead (which I can publish independently and won't require me to make public appearances) as a supplemental income kind of a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T13:19:07-08:00","id":68038,"title":"","content":"Not to discourage you, but I've heard from a couple of writers (can't remember exactly which ones) that everyone has about 5 years worth of bad writing in them. So expect rejection and take the criticism as a chance to get better. Also, keep all of that bad stuff with you. There may come a time when you've gotten legitimately good and can go back and look at some of your early stuff mine the good ideas out of it, change the writing up and end up with the awesome story you always knew it could be.<br /> <br /> Those are words given to me by a bunch o successful writers, all mashed up from fuzzy memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: Unless stated otherwise, all examples I give are completely random and almost assuredly pulled from my nethers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1575-dairugger","name":"Dairugger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/